===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:nedes|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|nedes|t=of necessity, necessarily; inevitably, unavoidably}}{{nb...|neds, nedez, nedis, nedys, nedysse, needes, needis, needs, neodes, (Early Middle English) nydes|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=nẹ̄des|pos=adv|id=MED29200}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|nēdes}}, {{m|ang|nīedes|t=of necessity; not willingly}}<!--, originally the {{glossary|genitive}} form of {{m|ang|nīed|t=necessity, need; distress}} – no such genitive existed since PG -->, from {{m|ang|nīed}} + {{m|ang|-es|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|adverb}}s from {{glossary|noun}}s}}.

The English word is equivalent to {{affix|en|need|-'s|pos2=possessive marker|nocat=1}} and hence to {{suffix|en|need|s|pos2=suffix forming adverbs|id2=adverbial}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=adv|id=125801|date=March 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adv}}</ref>

